 "basis": "script/m14/tmp/hs-local-identity.ts, one instrument, both runs, same draw (hledger 186 .hs + cabal 2,150 .hs): `before` = the analyzer at 35e80314 (bare local endpoints), `after` = the scoped-local identity round. `bareBinder` = an endpoint whose name equals a local binder name in the same file (the pre-fix local attribution); `localChain` = an endpoint whose head is a function/method symbol and whose tail is a local binder name (the scoped `owner.local` identity); `resolved` = endpoint is a file symbol; `bareUndeclared` = any other bare endpoint (constructors, imported names). Endpoint classification is rule-agnostic — it reads only emitted text, the symbol table and the tree's binder names — so both runs are comparable. Recorded refinement: the local-chain head test was tightened mid-round from `head is any symbol` to `head is a function/method symbol` after the first after-run let single-uppercase CONSTRUCTOR symbols (`data Side = L | R`) masquerade as owners; the before-side bucket is unaffected (its local-chain count was 0 by measurement, and dotted non-chain endpoints were unclassified under both spellings).",
